for macOS arm64 and x86_64. PDFium is Copyright 2014 The PDFium Authors and
is provided under the BSD-style terms in Vendor/PDFium/licenses/pdfium.txt.
The prebuilt binary packaging is Copyright 2014-2025 Benoit Blanchon and
is provided under the MIT terms in Vendor/PDFium/LICENSE. Additional bundled
libraries retain their respective notices in Vendor/PDFium/licenses/.
These third-party components are not relicensed under the project's MPL-2.0.

The application and release archives include the complete upstream LICENSE
and licenses directory at Contents/Resources/Legal/PDFium/. Binary provenance,
pinned version, and archive checksums are documented in Vendor/PDFium/README.md.

The offline AI response renderer includes KaTeX 0.19.0 (MIT), Marked 18.1.0
(MIT), and DOMPurify 3.4.16 (Apache-2.0 option of its dual license). Original
notices, licenses, pinned source locations, and integrity values are preserved
under Resources/AIRichText and shipped at Contents/Resources/AIRichText.
KaTeX's bundled WOFF2 fonts are covered by its accompanying MIT license.

The native raw-stream reader links against qpdf 12.4.1 (Apache-2.0) and
libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0. The libjpeg API used here carries the Independent JPEG
Group notice. This software is based in part on the work of the Independent
JPEG Group. The complete upstream licenses and notices are included in
Vendor/QPDF/licenses/ and in the app at Contents/Resources/Legal/QPDF/.
Pinned sources, the local qpdf patch, and rebuild instructions are listed
in Vendor/QPDF/README.md.
